From 4d37c540b15f15b5aa8cf4a7aa97a9e2ef9872ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <dev@infoverify.local>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 10:03:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Redesign LoginPage to match the CcHUB Gateway reference
 layout

Restructured to the layout shown in the reference screenshots (gateway.
cchub.africa/auth/login) - centered white card, bold "Welcome back"
heading, icon-in-input fields, a Remember me + Forgot password row,
and a full-width primary button with a "Register here!" link below -
while keeping MARIA's own established gold/ember/cream identity
(index.css literally documents this as "matches the Flutter app's
identity" - the reference's cream/orange is CcHUB's own brand, not
something to copy over).

- Email/password fields now show a leading icon (Mail/Lock, lucide-
  react) inside the input, matching the reference.
- Password field's show/hide toggle switched from a text button to an
  Eye/EyeOff icon button, same idea as the reference's eye icon.
- Added a "Remember me" checkbox next to "Forgot password?" (previously
  absent). Functional, not just decorative: when checked, the
  identifier (never the password/PIN) is saved to localStorage and
  pre-filled on the next visit - no backend or auth.tsx changes needed,
  login still goes through the normal flow every time.
- "Continue" as the primary button label (was "Sign in"), matching the
  reference; the PIN step keeps its own "Verify & sign in" label since
  that's a second, distinct step.
- Existing two-step login (identifier/password -> optional 6-digit PIN
  prompt) preserved as-is, just restyled to the same card.
- `Spinner` re-exported unchanged - ForgotPasswordPage, RegisterPage,
  and SetNewPasswordPage all import it from this file.

Verified: frontend tsc clean, vite build succeeds.
